{"edits": [{"finding_ids": ["app/geo.py:9:test-failure"], "search": "from pydantic.dataclasses import dataclass


class StrictConfig:
    anystr_strip_whitespace = True
    validate_assignment = True", "replace": "from pydantic import ConfigDict
from pydantic.dataclasses import dataclass


StrictConfig = ConfigDict(str_strip_whitespace=True, validate_assignment=True)", "explanation": "Pydantic V2 deprecates class-based `config` (PydanticDeprecatedSince20) in favor of `ConfigDict`. The v1 option `anystr_strip_whitespace` was renamed to `str_strip_whitespace` in V2, and `validate_assignment` is unchanged. `StrictConfig` keeps its name, so the existing `@dataclass(config=StrictConfig)` line works unchanged with the `ConfigDict` value, and any external imports of `StrictConfig` still resolve."}], "notes": "Only the class-based config (finding app/geo.py:9:test-failure) was migrated. The `@dataclass(config=StrictConfig)` line needed no change because it now receives a ConfigDict. Not changed, but needs human attention: `Point.__post_init_post_parse__` is a Pydantic v1 hook. Pydantic V2 dataclasses do not call it, so the coordinate range check and label title-casing will silently stop running. The V2 equivalent is `__post_init__`, which runs after validation. This was not in the listed findings, so I left it alone under the scope rule. Renaming it is a behavior-affecting change that should be verified against tests, e.g. with an out-of-range lat/lon test. Also, the 'pydantic-settings' note does not apply: this file has no BaseSettings usage. No Pydantic model classes exist in the repository, so the [needs-check] concern does not apply."}
